{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815603-the-lonely-girl-character-development","id":815603,"title":"The Lonely Girl (character development)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T11:59:40-08:00","id":815603,"title":"The Lonely Girl (character development)","content":"The concept is simple: A girl of six or seven is abducted, and taken to a domain composed of abandoned houses, abandoned hospitals, abandoned schools, abandoned libraries, etc. The key point is that everything is abandoned and empty, run-down and desolate. Well... almost. I'm assuming there were a few more-or-less intact places for the girl to bathe, and to shelter in. She was always able to scavenge food, and to find water, or else she'd be dead, and she probably managed to find clothes. Probably tattered and ill-fitting to suit the general aesthetic. Anyway, the girl manages to survive in this empty, desolate place for years by her measures, and keeps searching for a way out, finally finding a stone arch in a forest. She puts together clues from books in the abandoned libraries, and opens the gate, passing into the Hedge and from there, returning to the human world. She emerges in a play park, stepping out through a play structure's doorway. Apart from the obvious, that she'll be very badly socially impaired, what traits might suit this girl? Which Seeming and which Kith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:13:34-08:00","id":815610,"title":"","content":"Considering she apparently investigated her way out, probably a Wizened, in 2e. Not sure about the Kith; maybe something to do with silence/shadow or which benefits your Survival?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:15:40-08:00","id":815648,"title":"","content":"In 2e, Beast seeming (to reflect lack of social skills and living on your own for years).<br /> Farwalker Kith is perfect for this. The flavor text reads<i>: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Unlike many other Lost, a farwalker's Durance was not one of captivity but of near endless solitude and isolation. </span></span></i> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:30:09-08:00","id":815689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815603-the-lonely-girl-character-development?p=815648#post815648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, Beast seeming (to reflect lack of social skills and living on your own for years).<br /> Farwalker Kith is perfect for this. The flavor text reads<i>: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Unlike many other Lost, a farwalker's Durance was not one of captivity but of near endless solitude and isolation. </span></span></i> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the Kith, but not the Seeming. In 2e, your Seeming is not the nature of your Durance, but how you escaped/regained your agency. The Girl can't be a Beast, because that seems to focus on rebellion or shucking off the chains of society, and there was no society or authority to rebel against. <br /> Likewise, the Fairest are barred(no people) by the very circumstances. According to LadyLens, the Girl escaped through investigation and exploration, which seems to best fit the skill-based Wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:29:07-08:00","id":816859,"title":"","content":"So what Abilities might she have? There were plenty of books in the abandoned libraries, and I don't see much in the way of barriers to developing physical skills. Social skills would be... residual, leftovers from early childhood, but which ones in particular might be appropriate? Attributes would clearly be mental first, social last (who's she had to talk to?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 01-26-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:29:44-08:00","id":817262,"title":"","content":"High academics, with expertise in research. Better than average stamina. Were you wanting her to resemble a little girl, or the adult she would have been? For the little one, low strength, and with the adult, average everything with high stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T19:43:53-08:00","id":817345,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm assuming she aged at least a few years in biological terms, so she'd be mid to late teens or maybe young adult by the time she gets out. How much time passed between her abduction and return by Earthside measures is another question. Ste probably set up a &quot;nest&quot; of sorts in one of the more nearly intact houses, probably in a den or study with a fireplace. Somewhere she could make a fire for heat and cooking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}